# How often in Russian: иногда́, никогда́
subtitle: "Say how often you do things in Russian: всегда́, ча́сто, иногда́, ре́дко, never with its не (никогда́ не хожу́), and раз в неде́лю."
tags: ["russian","how often","frequency adverbs","никогда","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/frequency"]
thumb: "band \"Never needs a не\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Nothing and nobody in Russian: ничего́ не зна́ю","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/87-russian-negatives.cast"}

