  lines:
    '|a||How often in Russian: иногда́, никогда́':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Say how often you do things in Russian: всегда́, ча́сто, иногда́, ре́дко, never with its не (никогда́ не хожу́), and раз в неде́лю.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1qsw4q2'
    '|a||How do you say how often you do something in Russian? You can already say я хожу́ в парк ка́ждый день.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Today: always, never, and the words in between.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:14gxybu'
    '|a||Picture ten chances to go somewhere. Всегда́, always: all ten.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1k9mqn6'
    '|b||Я всегда́ е́зжу на рабо́ту на метро́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:1hwbunu'
    '|a||Ча́сто is often: most of them. Я ча́сто хожу́ в кино́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1i33dp6'
    '|b||Иногда́, sometimes: a few. Иногда́ я е́зжу к ба́бушке.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:13lvga0'
    '|a||Ре́дко, rarely: not often. Я ре́дко хожу́ в теа́тр.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:b31tvz'
    '|a||And no dots at all: никогда́, never.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1eas1f0'
    '|b||Я никогда́ не хожу́ в теа́тр.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2680
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:hrd9uc'
    '|a||Listen for the не. With никогда́, Russian says not as well: never, not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:oc3gyu'
    '|b||In English that''s a double negative; in Russian it''s the rule, and leaving out не is the mistake.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:z5mio8'
    '|a||Which word needs не before the verb?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1pzosde'
    '|a||Никогда́: я никогда́ не хожу́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2880
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Where do they go? Mostly just before the verb, or first: я ча́сто хожу́, иногда́ я е́зжу; or at the end, as an answer: в теа́тр я хожу́ ре́дко.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12040
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||And the verb is the habit one, хожу́ or е́зжу, not иду́, as with ка́ждый день in lesson sixty-two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:11tswln'
    '|a||To be exact, count the times: раз в неде́лю, once a week.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:s526ad'
    '|b||Неде́ля becomes неде́лю after в, as in че́рез неде́лю, and as суббо́та becomes в суббо́ту.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:4tz2p0'
    '|a||Twice is два ра́за, with the а from три ра́за в день: два ра́за в неде́лю.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:xl5888'
    '|a||And looking back, with ра́ньше: Ра́ньше я ча́сто ходи́л в кино́, а сейча́с ре́дко.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1p4ap4g'
    '|b||I used to go often, but now rarely: ходи́л, because it was a habit.':
